  "notes": "UK dance-pop with a strident, accented delivery. The drum block is the entry's: \"trop-house kick/clap with offbeat shaker and pitched-pluck hat substitute; the Clean-Bandit-adjacent records add a live-feel snare and string-section stabs on the backbeat.\" The pluck-instead-of-hat claim is authored as an 8th `hihat.base` at a low fill density with the roll vocabulary off, while the offbeat shaker is the perc lane at `offbeat` placement, and the kick sits on all four beats. The bass is a synth sub and no 808 is named, so no `bass808` block is authored; \"low end drops out for pre-choruses\" is the deep arrangement drop-out. Harmony is \"4-bar minor loops with 7ths\". The melody block is driven by the entry's hook claim — \"hooks are frequently a pitched instrumental riff answering the vocal\" — which is why the countermelody carries the highest `answer_lick` weight and the highest density ratio of any model in this batch: on these records the counter *is* the hook. \"Toplines are short-celled, syllabic, and written for chant-along\" is the 1—2 bar phrase and the small `motifPitchCount`; \"harmonies are close doubles\" is the +12 offset held. ⚠ `confidence` is medium and the research says the parameters are \"lane-conventional\": every drum probability, the humanize pair, the harmonic weights, the melody register and `bpm.mode` 115 (the midpoint of the stated 100—130 band) are INFERRED. ⚠ The entry's [LOW-CONF] mark on the vowel-placement/vocal claim is repeated here.",
